    "final_text": "The audit turned up one real bug, which is now fixed: `node index.js list | head -1` on a long list crashed with a stack trace when `head` closed the pipe early. The entry point now ignores that closed-pipe error (`EPIPE`) and exits normally (`index.js:102`). A new end-to-end test failed before the fix and passes after it (`test/e2e.test.js:100`). The fix is committed as `75785a8`.\n\nA second full review after the fix found nothing new. On the final code, lint is clean and all 100 tests pass.\n\nFour minor issues are recorded but not fixed:\n- Saving replaces a symlinked `todos.json`, or one with custom permissions, with a plain file.\n- Timestamps in a hand-edited file are checked only loosely.\n- A file saved with a byte-order mark (some Windows editors add one) is reported as corrupted.\n- Two commands writing at the same moment can lose one change. The README already says this.\n\nI wrote the completion receipt; the command printed nothing and returned no error.\n\nPROMPT_COMPLETE",
